From 4453afc273f5b65e47991ebaa7c39f07fafe163f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Remora <remora@localhost>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 08:52:18 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 13/16] venus: resolve imageless framebuffers, and publish only
 the compositor
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Fixes the host-encoded mirror showing the launcher's window instead of the
screen — app drawer over black, wallpaper missing (bd remora-e5x.15).

Per-context chain counters located the break to one link. SurfaceFlinger did
everything — 402 memory imports with res_ids, 402 images, 1995 views, 398
framebuffer bindings — with fb=0 and resolved=0, while the launcher resolved
352/400 on identical hooks. Verified cause: SF creates its framebuffers with
VK_FRAMEBUFFER_CREATE_IMAGELESS_BIT (measured flags=0x1; every app context uses
0x0), so vkCreateFramebuffer carries no views and the framebuffer->view map
never learns its target. The view arrives at vkCmdBeginRenderPass in
VkRenderPassAttachmentBeginInfo instead — a structure nothing read.

vkr_remora_note_rp_attachments() now takes attachment 0 from that pNext chain,
after VKR_CMD_CALL so the handles are already host handles. With it in place SF
resolves 597/600, at 3760x1992 — the composited display.

That makes positive identification possible, so the extent heuristic is retired:
only the context named by REMORA_COMPOSITOR (default "surfaceflinger") labels
and publishes. Extent-plus-activity had now been wrong four separate ways — a
dead publisher, a competing GL-pass producer, the launcher's own full-screen
window, and a stale label after resize — because any app can render at exactly
the display's size. The compositor's output is the mirror's frame by definition.
Setting REMORA_COMPOSITOR empty restores the old any-context behaviour for
non-Android guests.

Verified end to end in compose mode: exactly one publisher (surfaceflinger),
54.5 fps at 3760x1992, zero stream errors, and the captured frame is the
composited home screen — wallpaper and nav bar, not a window over black.

SF was invisible to earlier instrumentation for two reasons worth remembering:
every context log sat on the resolved path (circular), and the early lines went
to a log scrcpy's detached spawn truncates. The per-process announce now fires
on first submit, before any resolution.
